		GMOS TOP LEVEL SOFTWARE DIRECTORY
		=================================

This is the top level GMOS software directory. It contains the
GMOS Components Controller and Instrument Sequencer software.

The GMOS software and GMOS detector controller software are stored in a
"Universal Application Environment" (UAE) directory structure.

The top level GMOS directory contains the following tools in the form of
scripts:

gmosInstall    - Standard Gemini script for installing and building
                 the GMOS software. It also creates the "gmosdc"
                 pointer from the GMOS_DC environment variable.
                 gmosInstall carries out the same functions as a
                 uaeSetup followed by uaeTidy. The script creates a
                 gmosBuild.Log file.

gmosCshrc      - Setup script, to be included in a users .cshrc file,
                 which defines environment variables and aliases
                 necessary for running the GMOS software.

uaeSetup       - Original script for setting up the UAE environment for
                 the GMOS software. It also creates the "gmosdc"
                 pointer from the GMOS_DC environment variable.

uaeUnsetup     - Script to destroy all the built files and UAE
                 environment in the GMOS software

makeEverything - Script to build all the GMOS software.

uaeTidy        - Script to remove junk files interactively prior to
                 releasing the software.


The following commands are used to start the GMOS control screens, once a VME crate has been booted:

gmosStart <V>  - Script to start the GMOS control screens. The argument
                 <V> can be as follows.

                 MK (default) - Connect to real MK software.
                 SIM          - Connect to simulated MK software.
                 PRE          - Connect to MK software with simulated
				post focal plane and real pre focal
				plane.
                 POST         - Connect to MK software with simulated
				pre focal plane and real post focal
				plane.
                 CP           - Connect to real CP software.

                 The GMOS_MK_ACCESS or GMOS_CP_ACCESS environment
                 variables need to be defined before connecting to
                 MK or CP hardware (for safety reasons).

gmosAlarm <V>  - Script to start the GMOS alarm handler screen. The
                 argument <V> is the same as for gmosStart.


The following procedure makes and builds the GMOS software:

1) Untar the files (if they have been released in a tar archive)
   For example

      gunzip <gmos.tar.gz | tar -xvf -

2) Set up for EPICS software development by executing
   $EPICS/config/epics.csh and ~p3/capfastStart, or
   whatever.

3) Set up for GMOS software development

      source gmosCshrc

4) Execute the gmosInstall script in the top level directory.
